Article 3: Where a guarantee falls under any of the following circumstances, and a party claims that the nature of the guarantee is an independent letter of guarantee, the People's Court shall support such claim, except where the guarantee does not specify the documents based on which payment is to be made and the maximum amount:
(1) The guarantee specifies payment on demand;
(2) The guarantee specifies the application of model rules for independent guarantee transactions such as the Uniform Rules for Demand Guarantees of the International Chamber of Commerce;
(3) According to the text of the guarantee, the issuer's payment obligation is independent of the underlying transaction relationship and the legal relationship of the guarantee application, and it only bears the payment liability for complying presentation.
Where a party claims that the guarantee is a general suretyship or joint and several suretyship on the ground that the independent letter of guarantee records the corresponding underlying transaction, the People's Court shall not support such claim.
Where a party claims that the independent letter of guarantee is subject to the provisions of the Civil Code on general suretyship or joint and several suretyship, the People's Court shall not support such claim.

Article 11: Where an independent letter of guarantee falls under any of the following circumstances, and a party claims that the rights and obligations under the independent letter of guarantee are terminated, the People's Court shall support such claim:
(1) The expiry date or expiry event specified in the independent letter of guarantee has arrived, and the beneficiary has not presented documents conforming to the requirements of the independent letter of guarantee;
(2) All amounts payable under the independent letter of guarantee have been fully paid;
(3) The amount of the independent letter of guarantee has been reduced to zero;
(4) The issuer has received a document issued by the beneficiary releasing the payment obligation under the independent letter of guarantee;
(5) Other circumstances under which termination is provided by law or agreed by the parties.
Where an independent letter of guarantee falls under the circumstances of termination of rights and obligations in the preceding paragraph, and the beneficiary claims to have the right to request payment on the ground that it holds the text of the independent letter of guarantee, the People's Court shall not support such claim.

Article 12: Where any of the following circumstances exists, the People's Court shall determine that fraud in an independent letter of guarantee is constituted:
(1) The beneficiary colludes with the guarantee applicant or other persons to fabricate the underlying transaction;
(2) The third-party documents presented by the beneficiary are forged or have false contents;
(3) A court judgment or arbitral award determines that the debtor under the underlying transaction has no payment or compensation liability;
(4) The beneficiary confirms that the debt under the underlying transaction has been fully performed or confirms that the payment maturity event specified in the independent letter of guarantee has not occurred;
(5) Other circumstances where the beneficiary, knowing that it has no right to request payment, still abuses such right.

Article 14: The People's Court shall issue a ruling to suspend payment of the amount under an independent letter of guarantee only if all of the following conditions are simultaneously met:
(1) The evidence materials submitted by the applicant for suspension of payment prove that the existence of the circumstances under Article 12 of these Provisions is highly probable;
(2) The situation is urgent, and failure to immediately take suspension measures would cause irreparable damage to the lawful rights and interests of the applicant for suspension of payment;
(3) The applicant for suspension of payment has provided security sufficient to compensate the respondent for losses that may be suffered due to the suspension of payment.
Where the applicant for suspension of payment requests suspension on the ground that the beneficiary has breached the contract in the underlying transaction, the People's Court shall not support such request.
Where the issuer has already made payment in good faith under an independent letter of guarantee issued upon instruction, the People's Court shall not rule to suspend payment on the independent letter of guarantee that secures the right of recourse of such issuer.
